<!--
  Types that Lisp asks for by name.

  The trimmer sees no IL referring to any of this: a core is loaded at run time
  and reaches .NET through strings, so a type nothing else happens to use is
  removed and the call fails at boot with MissingMethodException. Rooting whole
  assemblies is not an option here — System.Private.CoreLib is most of the
  download — so the types are named one at a time.

  The list came from scanning the sources in the image for "System.*" literals,
  not from reading code. Rescan when the image changes.

    System.Runtime.InteropServices.OSPlatform
    System.Runtime.InteropServices.RuntimeInformation
        trivial-features (src/tf-dotcl.lisp) and cffi (src/cffi-dotcl.lisp)
        ask which OS and architecture they are on while they load, through
        RuntimeInformation.IsOSPlatform against each OSPlatform value in turn.

  Both live in System.Private.CoreLib here: the facade assemblies that normally
  export them are not part of a browser-wasm bundle.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="System.Private.CoreLib">
    <type fullname="System.Runtime.InteropServices.OSPlatform" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="System.Runtime.InteropServices.RuntimeInformation" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
